algorithm on a lattice of dimension~$105$ in approximately 30 minutes. The
algorithm derived from \cite{peng2014} factored two balanced 1024-bit
semi-primes ($\alpha=512$, $t=490$) by running the LLL algorithm on a lattice of
dimension $105$ in approximately $13.75$ hours.

In 2015 Peng, Hu, Lu, Huang, and Xu \cite{peng2015} adapted the algorithm
